Again, climb the tower and touch the gems to move along.  In the first warp\
space, you get a little puzzle.  Each of the brightly-lit corner blocks rises\
when you walk on it.  You have to raise all of them and end up in the middle of\
the West row, where the walkway to the exit will appear.  Here is one possible\
order to do them in:\
                            exit\
                             ^^\
Walk on the blocks       F--G--B--A               W\
in the order numbered,   |  |  |  |               |\
from 1-9, then A-G.      E--D--C--9            S--+--N\
                         |  |  |  |               |\
                         3--4--5--8               E\
                         |  |  |  |\
                         2--1--6--7\
                             ^^\
                        Start here\
\
In the next warp space, you have to repeat the pattern you are shown, by\
stepping on the squares in the same order.  On the first try, the pattern is as\
follows:\
                 4 - 9 - 1           W\
                 |   |   |           |\
                 8 - 2 - 7        S--+--N\
                 |   |   |           |\
                 3 - 5 - 6           E\
\
If you miss the first time, then the pattern changes, so you just have to try\
and memorize it, or draw the pattern as it lights up, then walk on the squares\
in the same order.  Keep on going to reach this pillar's mid-boss.  **Thanks to\
Michael L. for catching a typo in the puzzle solution just above, where I\
originally had the number 5 appearing twice.**\
